      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong><span>This post is written in Spanish on purpose. You don’t need to understand every word; just keep reading.</span></strong></p><p>Mi amiga Mercedes, y fiel lectora de esta cuenta, me dio el otro día una idea estupenda.</p><div class="subscription-widget-wrap-editor" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://dailypushes.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}" data-component-name="SubscribeWidgetToDOM"><div class="subscription-widget show-subscribe"><div class="preamble"><p class="cta-caption">Thanks for reading Daily Push(es)! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.</p></div><form class="subscription-widget-subscribe"><input type="email" class="email-input" name="email" placeholder="Type your email…" tabindex="-1"><input type="submit" class="button primary" value="Subscribe"><div class="fake-input-wrapper"><div class="fake-input"></div><div class="fake-button"></div></div></form></div></div><p>¿Por qué no escribes sobre la familia? A veces se me olvidan los parentescos en español.</p><p>Y pensé: pues tiene toda la razón.</p><p> <em>Madre</em>, <em>padre</em> o <em>hermano</em>, se aprenden rápido, pero otra muy distinta es acordarse de quién es el <strong>cuñado</strong>, la <strong>nuera</strong>, el <strong>suegro</strong> o el <strong>sobrino</strong>.</p><p>Hay que reconocer que en español los parentescos son bastante más variados que en inglés.</p><p>Así que hoy vamos a repasarlos con una familia que seguro que conocéis.</p><p>Sí, la familia real británica.</p><div class="captioned-image-container"><figure><a class="image-link image2 is-viewable-img" target="_blank" href="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HUOc!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F03888fa3-ca21-4e41-be69-35f3ebcad2a8_1536x1024.png" data-component-name="Image2ToDOM"><div class="image2-inset"><picture><source type="image/webp" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HUOc!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F03888fa3-ca21-4e41-be69-35f3ebcad2a8_1536x1024.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HUOc!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F03888fa3-ca21-4e41-be69-35f3ebcad2a8_1536x1024.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HUOc!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F03888fa3-ca21-4e41-be69-35f3ebcad2a8_1536x1024.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HUOc!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F03888fa3-ca21-4e41-be69-35f3ebcad2a8_1536x1024.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw"><img src="https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/03888fa3-ca21-4e41-be69-35f3ebcad2a8_1536x1024.png" width="1456" height="971" data-attrs="{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/03888fa3-ca21-4e41-be69-35f3ebcad2a8_1536x1024.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:971,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:1533496,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://dailypushes.substack.com/i/208657327?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F03888fa3-ca21-4e41-be69-35f3ebcad2a8_1536x1024.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}" class="sizing-normal" alt="" srcset="https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HUOc!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F03888fa3-ca21-4e41-be69-35f3ebcad2a8_1536x1024.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HUOc!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F03888fa3-ca21-4e41-be69-35f3ebcad2a8_1536x1024.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HUOc!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F03888fa3-ca21-4e41-be69-35f3ebcad2a8_1536x1024.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HUOc!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F03888fa3-ca21-4e41-be69-35f3ebcad2a8_1536x1024.png 1456w" sizes="auto, 100vw" loading="lazy"></picture><div class="image-link-expand"><div class="pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset"><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg aria-hidden="true" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="var(--color-fg-primary)" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-noB79L"><g><path d="M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex="0" type="button" class="pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L"><polyline points="15 3 21 3 21 9"></polyline><polyline points="9 21 3 21 3 15"></polyline><line x1="21" x2="14" y1="3" y2="10"></line><line x1="3" x2="10" y1="21" y2="14"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p></p><p>Voy a intentar explicarlo de la forma más sencilla posible. No prometo nada. 😄</p><p>Isabel II y Felipe eran marido y mujer y tuvieron cuatro hijos, ocho nietos y doce bisnietos.</p><p>La madre de Carlos III era Isabel II y su padre, Felipe.</p><p>Carlos III tiene una hermana, Ana, y dos hermanos, Andrés y Eduardo.</p><p>Carlos está casado con Camilla. Eso significa que Ana es su <strong>cuñada</strong>, y Andrés y Eduardo son sus <strong>cuñados</strong>.</p><p>Además, Carlos tiene dos <strong>nueras</strong>: Catalina y Meghan.</p><p>Y también es abuelo de los hijos de Guillermo y Enrique.</p><p>Por otro lado, Isabel II era la <strong>suegra</strong> de Camilla, y Felipe, su <strong>suegro</strong>.</p><p>Guillermo y Enrique son hermanos y, por tanto, los hijos de cada uno son los <strong>sobrinos</strong> del otro.</p><p>Es decir, Guillermo es el <strong>tío</strong> de los hijos de Enrique, y Enrique es el <strong>tío</strong> de los hijos de Guillermo.</p><p>¿Me sigues?</p><p>Porque yo he tenido que releerlo un par de veces para asegurarme de que no me estaba liando. 😂</p><p>¿Cuál es para ti la palabra de la familia que siempre se te olvida?</p><p>Y ya que estamos, aprovecho para preguntarte si hay algún tema de gramática o vocabulario que te gustaría que explicara por aquí. Cuéntamelo en los comentarios. Muchas de las ideas para estos artículos salen precisamente de conversaciones como la que tuve con Mercedes.</p><p class="button-wrapper" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://dailypushes.substack.com/p/spanish-family-vocabulary-made-simple?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}" data-component-name="ButtonCreateButton"><a class="button primary" href="https://dailypushes.substack.com/p/spanish-family-vocabulary-made-simple?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share"><span>Share</span></a></p><p><span>One last thing 😊</span></p><p><span>If you enjoyed this article, I’d be incredibly grateful if you tapped the ❤️ below.</span></p><p><span>¡Hasta la semana que viene! </span></p><p><span>Myriam</span></p><p></p><div class="subscription-widget-wrap-editor" data-attrs="{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://dailypushes.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}" data-component-name="SubscribeWidgetToDOM"><div class="subscription-widget show-subscribe"><div class="preamble"><p class="cta-caption">Thanks for reading Daily Push(es)! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.</p></div><form class="subscription-widget-subscribe"><input type="email" class="email-input" name="email" placeholder="Type your email…" tabindex="-1"><input type="submit" class="button primary" value="Subscribe"><div class="fake-input-wrapper"><div class="fake-input"></div><div class="fake-button"></div></div></form></div></div>]]></content:encoded>
